  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday Night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1150 AM CST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\nThe big high pressure system will move east and center near the \nMid Atlantic on Wednesday which coincides with ridging aloft \nmoving into the Tennessee and Ohio Valleys. A more noticeable \nwarm-up will proceed with afternoon highs into the 70s west of \nthe Plateau by Friday. Overnight lows will remain above freezing \nmid to late week. It appears we'll transition into a more \nprogressive pattern by the weekend and this will feature a \nnorthern stream shortwave trough and associated cold front moving \ninto the region. NBM guidance remains consistent with a low \nchance for rain on Sunday with individual model disagreement \nregarding how much moisture will be along the front and how \namplified the trough will be (for forcing). Some guidance is more\nsuggestive of a light/moderate soaking rainfall area-wide, and \nsome remain quite dry. A dose of rain would be nice. Either way, a\ncool-down will come behind the cold front which would carry cool\ntemperatures into early next week.",
